<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carpenter Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carpenter Agreement was signed on 22 March 1915 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frank-carpenter">Frank W. Carpenter</a>, American governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> and Sulu, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamalul-kiram-ii">Jamalul Kiram II</a> of Sulu. The sultan gave up all temporal power and claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, while remaining head of the Muslim religion in Sulu. It ended the Sulu Sultanate as a political authority.</p></div>
